tion {:value "127565"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "128336"} "1980"] "\n" [:option {:value "129090"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "130094"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "131219"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "132293"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "133209"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "133842"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "263316"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "332506"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "19009561"} "2020"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008041"} "2024"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/675"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Light-Heavyweight, Freestyle (≤86 kg), Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "20 August 2016"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/902"} "Arena Carioca 2, Parque Olímpico da Barra, Barra da Tijuca, Rio de Janeiro"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/355358"} "19 from 19 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Single elimination tournament. Competitors losing to the finalists entered repechage tournament for bronze medals."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} [:a {:href "/athletes/135824"} "Abdul-Rashid Sadulayev"] " of Russia was the heavy gold medal favorite entering the Rio Olympic Games, after winning the last two consecutive World Championships (2014, 2015) where he surrendered a total of four points in those tournaments; and had an impressive win-loss career record of 58-1 over the last four years. Posed to challenge Sadulayev was defending Olympic champion and 2011 World champion Azerbaijan’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/121432"} "Şərif Şərifov"] ", and two-time World medalist " [:a {:href "/athletes/136152"} "Selim Yasar"] " of Turkey, " [:a {:href "/athletes/117097"} "Reineris Salas"] " of Cuba, and international newcomer, " [:a {:href "/athletes/136402"} "J’den Cox"] " of the United States, the two-time NCAA champion."] "\n\n" [:p {} "En-route to the final bout in the 86 kg class, Sadulayev had not given up one single point in the Olympic tournament, outscoring three early opponents 28-0. In his semi-final bout against Şərifov, Sadulayev, known as the “Russian Tank”, gave up one single point, beating Şərifov 8-1 (the only point won against him the entire Olympic tournament)."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Considered to be the best pound-for-pound wrestler alive, Sadulayev, who entered the Olympic Games undefeated since 2013, met Yaşar in the gold medal match - a repeat of the 2015 World Championship final in Las Vegas, won by Sadulayev. Yasar had advanced to the final after beating American Cox 3-1."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the final, Sadulayev scored on a pair of two-point moves late in the first period, ultimately beating Yasar 5-0 for the second year in a row in a major tournament, and his capturing his third straight global title."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Bronze medals went to Şərifov and Cox (who scored a take-down with six seconds left to give the United States its first freestyle medal of the Rio Games.)"] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Classification Points", :class "footnote"} "CP"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Victories by Fall", :class "footnote"} "VF"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Victories by Technical Superiority", :class "footnote"} "ST"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Technical Points", :class "footnote"} "TP"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Technical Points Received", :class "footnote"} "TPR"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""}